#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile fermionic circuits {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The concepts in this guide are currently available only in the Python API. Equivalent functionality will be made available in the C API in a future release.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide explains how to transpile a "
"[`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") to a standard "
"[`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)."
" It continues with the same time evolution example from the [fermionic "
"circuits guide](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation stages {#transpilation-stages}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As explained in "
"[`qiskit_fermions.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/transpiler#module-qiskit_fermions.transpiler "
"\"qiskit_fermions.transpiler\"), the preset pass managers in this project "
"split the transpilation into the following stages:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Input** {#input}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Converts the input circuit to a directed acyclic graph (DAG) data "
"structure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Optimization** {#optimization}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keeps the circuit in fermionic space. These passes use fermionic structure "
"and commutation relations while problem-aware knowledge remains fully "
"available. [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/transpiler-"
"passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis "
"\"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") is the pass that "
"Trotterizes an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution"
" \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate here, with a product "
"formula or with [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-"
"drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), and "
"[`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-"
"trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization "
"\"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") its occupation-"
"aware variant; see [Optimization "
"Passes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-"
"passes#qiskit-fermions-transpiler-passes-optimization) for the full set and "
"[Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-"
"synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation) for how a product formula is "
"chosen.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Layout** {#layout}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Maps fermionic mode registers to quantum registers. For occupation-basis "
"mappings like Jordan-Wigner, each fermionic mode maps to a single qubit. "
"This stage also supports more general mappings where the number of qubits "
"differs from the number of fermionic modes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Synthesis** {#synthesis}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Converts fermionic gates to qubit operations by using the chosen fermion-to-"
"qubit mapping. [`FermionicGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-fermionic-gate#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate\") instances are transformed into "
"sequences of standard quantum gates. A barrier is carried through onto every"
" qubit of each register it touched, so it continues to separate the gates on"
" either side of it during the qubit stage.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Qubit** {#qubit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transpiles the resulting qubit circuit by using standard Qiskit methods, "
"including optimization, layout, and routing for your target hardware.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Output** {#output}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the internal DAG data structure to the desired output format.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A practical example: transpilation using Jordan-Wigner {#a-practical-"
"example-transpilation-using-jordan-wigner}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the preset pass manager to transpile your fermionic circuit with the "
"Jordan-Wigner fermion-to-qubit mapping:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs group=\"tab\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit import FermionicCircuit\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit.library import Evolution\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets import generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Create the same fermionic circuit from the previous guide\n"
"    >>> circuit = FermionicCircuit(4)\n"
"    >>> hamiltonian = FermionOperator.from_terms([\n"
"    ...     ([cre(0), ann(2)], 0.5),\n"
"    ...     ([cre(2), ann(0)], 0.5),\n"
"    ...     ([cre(1), ann(3)], 0.5),\n"
"    ...     ([cre(3), ann(1)], 0.5),\n"
"    ... ])\n"
"    >>> hamiltonian.groups = [0, 0, 1, 1]\n"
"    >>> evolution = Evolution(4, hamiltonian, time=1.0)\n"
"    >>> circuit.append(evolution, circuit.register)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Generate the Jordan-Wigner transpilation pipeline\n"
"    >>> pm = generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Transpile the fermionic circuit to a qubit circuit\n"
"    >>> qubit_circuit = pm.run(circuit)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # The result is a standard QuantumCircuit\n"
"    >>> print(type(qubit_circuit))\n"
"    <class 'qiskit.circuit.quantumcircuit.QuantumCircuit'>\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // The C API for transpilation will be made available in a future release.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

